his.\n\nI need to ensure that each task uses the correct module and parameters as specified. Also, the YAML formatting must be correct to pass yamllint and ansible-lint checks. I'll structure each task with the appropriate module, action, and any necessary arguments.\n\nI should also make sure that the playbook starts with '---' followed by the tasks in the specified order without any additional comments or explanations, as per the user's request.\n\nNow, putting it all together, I'll write each task in YAML, ensuring that the syntax is correct and that all required fields are included. I'll double-check each task to confirm that the modules and parameters match the descriptions provided.\n\nFinally, I'll review the entire playbook to ensure there are no typos or formatting issues that could cause linting errors. This should result in a valid Ansible Playbook that meets all the specified requirements.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: cadvisor | create directories\n  file:\n    path: /var/lib/cadvisor\n    state: directory\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n    mode: 0755\n\n- name: cadvisor | download\n  uri:\n    url: https://example.com/cadvisor-amd64\n    dest: /usr/local/cadvisor/cadvisor-amd64\n    remote_src: yes\n    checksum: sha256:1234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef1234567890\n\n- name: cadvisor | propagate locally distributed cadvisor binary\n  copy:\n    src: /usr/local/cadvisor/cadvisor-amd64\n    dest: /usr/local/bin/cadvisor\n    remote_src: yes\n    notify: restart_cadvisor\n\n- name: cadvisor | symlink\n  ln:\n    src: /usr/local/bin/cadvisor\n    dest: /usr/bin/cadvisor\n    state: symlink\n\n- name: cadvisor | server systemd service\n  template:\n    src: cadvisor.service.j2\n    dest: /etc/systemd/system/cadvisor.service\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n    mode: 0644\n\n- name: test_task\n  command: systemctl status cadvisor\n  register: service_active\n\n- name: debug: var=service_active\n  debug:\n    var: service_active\n\n- name: cadvisor |