content="<think>\nAlright, I need to create an Ansible Playbook based on the given tasks. Let me go through each task one by one to ensure I understand what's required.\n\nFirst, the playbook must start with '---' on the first line. That's straightforward. Then, each task should be a YAML block with the specified name and module.\n\nTask 1 is to check if EFI firmware exists by checking the /sys/firmware/efi/efivars/ directory. I'll use the stat module with the path and check if the state is 'file'. The register will store the result for later tasks.\n\nNext, Task 2 deletes the GRUB config if EFI exists. Using the file module with state=absent makes sense. I'll conditionally run this only when the efi_firmware fact is true.\n\nFor Task 3, I need to copy a template to /etc/grub.d/01_users. The template module is appropriate here, ensuring the correct permissions and ownership.\n\nTask 4 and 5 involve modifying GRUB config files for EFI and MBR systems, respectively. I'll use the lineinfile module to insert the password lines. Again, these are conditional based on the efi_firmware fact.\n\nLastly, Task 6 adds unrestricted access to GRUB password entries. Another lineinfile task, ensuring the --unrestricted flag is added.\n\nI need to make sure all tasks are in the correct order and that each uses the right conditionals. Also, the YAML must be valid, so proper indentation and syntax are crucial. I'll avoid any unnecessary comments or headers as per the instructions.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Check if EFI firmware exists on the system\n  stat:\n    path: /sys/firmware/efi/efivars/\n    state: file\n  register: efi_firmware\n\n- name: Remove GRUB configuration file on EFI systems\n  file:\n    path: /boot/grub2/grub.cfg\n    state: absent\n  condition: efi_firmware.stat.exists\n\n- name: Install custom user template for GRUB\n  template:\n    src: 01_users.j2\n    dest: /etc/grub.d/01_users\n    mode: 0644\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n\n- name: Add EFI password protection to GRUB\n  lineinfile:\n    path: /etc/grub2-efi.cfg\n    line: password_pbkdf2 {{ grub_password }}\n    condition: efi_firmware.stat.exists\n\n- name: Add MBR password protection to GRUB\n  lineinfile:\n    path: /etc/grub2.cfg\n    line: password_pbkdf2 {{ grub_password }}\n    condition: not efi_firmware.stat.exists\n\n- name: Add unrestricted access to GRUB password entries\n  lineinfile:\n    path: /etc/grub2.cfg\n    line: set superusers=unrestricted\n    insertafter: password_pbkdf2 {{ grub_password }}\n```" additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-19T15:47:04.605102751Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 12260479354, 'load_duration': 100219612, 'prompt_eval_count': 468, 'prompt_eval_duration': 144436772, 'eval_count': 628, 'eval_duration': 12013869546, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--68e90c58-5509-4b1f-8c65-35f7eec72f37-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 468, 'output_tokens': 628, 'total_tokens': 1096}
