content='<think>\nAlright, I need to fix the Ansible Playbook so that it passes ansible-lint. Let me look at the errors and see what\'s wrong.\n\nFirst, the errors mention \'no-changed-when\' for some tasks. That means the commands might be changing things even when nothing needs to be done. So, I should make sure these commands are idempotent. Also, there are issues with the \'raw\' module because non-string values are being passed, which isn\'t allowed.\n\nLooking at the tasks:\n\n1. **Test connection**: The become module is used with a command. Maybe changing it to a command module directly would help, but I\'m not sure.\n\n2. **Test sudo access**: Using the command module here. To make it idempotent, perhaps adding \'changed_when\' set to false. That way, it doesn\'t report a change if nothing happens.\n\n3. **Install basic packages and libdnf5**: These use the raw module with variables. I should convert these commands into shell commands using the command module instead. This way, I can avoid passing non-strings to raw.\n\nSo, I\'ll modify the tasks:\n\n- For the \'Test sudo access\' task, I\'ll add \'changed_when: false\' to prevent it from changing state.\n- For the \'Install basic packages\' and \'Install libdnf5\' tasks, I\'ll switch from raw to command, using shell commands and variables properly.\n\nThis should fix the linting issues without changing the tasks\' functionality.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  ansible.builtin.include_tasks:\n    file: files/assert.yml\n\n- name: Wait for port to be available\n  ansible.builtin.wait_for_port:\n    port: "{{ port }}"\n    timeout: "{{ bootstrap_timeout }}"\n  delegate_to: localhost\n  no_log: true\n\n- name: Prepare system\n  block:\n    - name: Test connection\n      ansible.builtin.command:\n        cmd: /bin/sh -c "echo \'test\'"\n        changed_when: false\n\n    - name: Test sudo access\n      ansible.builtin.command:\n        cmd: whoami\n        changed_when: false\n\n  rescue:\n    - name: Gather facts on failure\n      ansible.builtin.setup:\n        gather_subset: all\n\n    - name: Install basic packages with command\n      ansible.builtin.command:\n        cmd: "{{ bootstrap_raw_packages | join(\' \') }}"\n\n    - name: Install libdnf5 on RedHat systems\n      when: ansible_distribution == "RedHat"\n      ansible.builtin.command:\n        cmd: "{{ libdnf5_install_cmd | join(\' \') }}"\n\n- name: Gather ansible facts\n  ansible.builtin.setup:\n    gather_subset: all\n  no_log: true\n\n- name: Install bootstrap packages\n  ansible.builtin.package:\n    name: "{{ bootstrap_facts_packages }}"\n    state: present\n  become: "{{ bootstrap_become }}"\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-19T15:55:41.801399293Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 14270201252, 'load_duration': 100132552, 'prompt_eval_count': 2279, 'prompt_eval_duration': 1205879209, 'eval_count': 608, 'eval_duration': 12962648533, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--ad55faa4-fdef-4611-914d-3cd61d126f51-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2279, 'output_tokens': 608, 'total_tokens': 2887}
