th correct indentation and no trailing spaces.\n\nWait, in the second task, the condition is when the variable py3ver is defined. In Ansible, variables are automatically registered if they exist, so I don\'t need to check if they are defined; if the first task ran, py3ver should exist. But the task description says to use when py3ver is defined, so I\'ll include that condition.\n\nAlso, in the command task, I should make sure that the command is correctly quoted to handle any spaces, but since it\'s a simple command, it should be fine.\n\nPutting it all together, the playbook will have two tasks under the tasks list. Each task is a dictionary with the module name, command, register, changed_when, and tags.\n\nI think that\'s all. Now, I\'ll write the YAML accordingly.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Check Python3 version on Debian12\n  command: python3 --version\n  register: py3ver\n  changed_when: false\n  tags:\n    - molecule-notest\n\n- name: Remove EXTERNALLY-MANAGED file on Debian12\n  file:\n    path: /usr/lib/python3.11/EXTERNALLY-MANAGED\n    state: absent\n  when:\n    - py3ver is defined\n    - "3.11" in py3ver.stdout\n  tags:\n    - molecule-notest\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-19T16:35:10.376023038Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 15630542182, 'load_duration': 106535152, 'prompt_eval_count': 387, 'prompt_eval_duration': 98812153, 'eval_count': 775, 'eval_duration': 15423978530, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--308cb300-5919-46f7-a20b-36567d4ade6b-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 387, 'output_tokens': 775, 'total_tokens': 1162}
