roper permissions and ownership.\n\nI need to make sure each task is in the correct order and uses the right modules. Also, I should avoid using hosts:, vars:, and other playbook-level headers since it's meant for a role.\n\nWait, for the group and user, I should ensure they're not root. Maybe specify shell for the user as /bin/false to prevent login.\n\nIn the config and application directories, setting the owner to promtail and correct permissions is important.\n\nWhen downloading and copying files, I should set remote_src to no if I'm copying from local, but for get_url, it's downloading from a URL, so maybe remote_src isn't needed.\n\nFor the symlink, I need to set the correct path and target. Maybe the binary is in /usr/local/bin, so the symlink would point to the latest version.\n\nI should also make sure that each task has the correct parameters. For example, in the user module, maybe set home directory to /home/promtail.\n\nIn the file module for directories, set mode to 755 to ensure correct permissions.\n\nFor the config and app directories, the ownership should be promtail and mode 755 as well.\n\nIn the binary existence check, using stat and register the result, then maybe in the next tasks, use that variable to conditionally proceed.\n\nBut since the user asked for all tasks to be included without conditions, I'll just list them in order.\n\nI think that's all. Now, I'll structure each task with the correct module and arguments.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Install unzip package\n  apt:\n    name: unzip\n    state: present\n\n- name: Create system group for promtail\n  group:\n    name: promtail\n    state: present\n\n- name: Create system user for promtail\n  user:\n    name: promtail\n    group: promtail\n    state: present\n    create_home: yes\n    shell: /bin/false\n\n- name: Ensure /usr/local/bin directory exists\n  file:\n    path: /usr/local/bin\n    state: directory\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n    mode: 755\n\n- name: Create config directories\n  file:\n    path: /etc/promtail\n    state: directory\n    owner: promtail\n    group: promtail\n    mode: 755\n\n- name: Create application directories\n  file:\n    path: /var/lib/promtail\n    state: directory\n    owner: promtail\n    group: promtail\n    mode: 755\n\n- name: Check promtail binary existence\n  stat:\n    path: /usr/local/bin/promtail\n    register: promtail_binary_exists\n\n- name: Download promtail binaries\n  get_url:\n    url: https://distribution.url/promtail-linux-amd64.zip\n    dest: /tmp/promtail-linux-amd64.zip\n    checksum: 'md5:abcdef1234567890'\n\n- name: Propagate local promtail binaries\n  copy:\n    src: /path/to/local/binary\n    dest: /tmp/\n    remote_src: no\n\n- name: Download promtail binaries for controller node\n  get_url:\n    url: https://distribution.url/promtail-controller-linux-amd64.zip\n    dest: /tmp/promtail-controller-linux-amd64.zip\n    checksum: 'md5:0123456789abcdef'\n\n- name: Propagate promtail binaries\n  copy:\n    src: /path/to/controller/binary\n    dest: /tmp/\n    remote_src: no\n\n- name: Unpack promtail binaries\n  unzip:\n    name: /tmp/promtail-linux-amd64.zip\n    dest: /usr/local/bin/\n\n- name: Create symlink to latest promtail version\n  file:\n    path: /usr/local/bin/promtail\n    state: lnk_file\n    src: /usr/local/bin/promtail-latest\n\n- name: Write promtail config file\n  template:\n    src: promtail-config.j2\n    dest: /etc/promtail/config.yml\n    owner: promtail\n    group: promtail\n    mode: 644\n\n- name: Create systemd service unit\n  template:\n    src: promtail.service.j2\n    dest: /etc/systemd/system/promtail.service\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n    mode: 644\n```" additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-19T16:58:36.519032036Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 29611254541, 'load_duration': 93964507, 'prompt_eval_count': 693, 'prompt_eval_duration': 377207854, 'eval_count': 1390, 'e