content='<think>\nOkay, so I\'ve got this Ansible playbook that\'s failing ansible-lint. Let\'s see what the errors are and how to fix them. The user provided the original playbook and the error messages, so I\'ll start by looking at those.\n\nFirst, the errors mention using FQCN for built-in modules like \'package\' and \'template\'. I remember that Ansible modules should be referenced with their fully qualified names to avoid ambiguity, especially when dealing with both ansible.builtin and ansible.legacy modules. So, I need to update the module names to their FQCNs.\n\nLooking at the first task, it\'s using \'package\' as the module. The error suggests using \'ansible.builtin.package\' instead. So, I\'ll change that line.\n\nNext, the second task uses \'template\' as the module. The same applies here; I should replace it with \'ansible.builtin.template\'.\n\nThen, there are two errors about forbidden implicit octal values. The playbook uses \'0644\' as a mode. Ansible now prefers using integers for mode, so I should convert \'0644\' to 412 (since 0644 in octal is 412 in decimal). Alternatively, I can use quotes to keep it as a string if that\'s acceptable, but using an integer is better practice.\n\nWait, looking at the error message, it says "Forbidden implicit octal value \'0644\'". So, using \'0644\' as a string is not allowed anymore. The correct way is to use the integer 412. I\'ll need to update both instances where \'0644\' is used.\n\nAlso, I should check if there are any other issues. The notifications in the tasks are correct, I think. They\'re notifying the handlers properly.\n\nSo, to summarize, the fixes are:\n\n1. Replace \'package\' with \'ansible.builtin.package\' in Task 1.\n2. Replace \'template\' with \'ansible.builtin.template\' in both Task 2 and Task 3.\n3. Change the \'mode\' parameter from \'0644\' to 412 in both template tasks.\n\nI\'ll go through each task and make these changes. Let me make sure I don\'t alter anything else, like the variables or task names, as per the instructions.\n\nNow, putting it all together, the corrected playbook should have the FQCN modules and the correct mode values. I\'ll structure it as YAML, ensuring proper indentation and formatting to pass ansible-lint.\n</think>\n\n---\n- name: Install SSL packages\n  ansible.builtin.package:\n    name: "{{ httpd_ssl_packages }}"\n    state: present\n\n- name: Place configuration\n  ansible.builtin.template:\n    src: ssl.conf.j2\n    dest: "{{ httpd_config_directory }}/ssl.conf"\n    mode: 412\n  notify:\n    - Test httpd configuration validity\n    - Restart httpd\n\n- name: Configure redirect from http to https\n  ansible.builtin.template:\n    src: default_vhost.conf.j2\n    dest: "{{ httpd_config_directory }}/{{ default_vhost_conf }}"\n    mode: 412\n  notify:\n    - Test httpd configuration validity\n    - Restart httpd' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-19T17:16:34.527738577Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 15384641468, 'load_duration': 83716010, 'prompt_eval_count': 1841, 'prompt_eval_duration': 1151707824, 'eval_count': 682, 'eval_duration': 14147563599, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--db65bc4a-b694-476e-99b7-aaaa750cd245-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 1841, 'output_tokens': 682, 'total_tokens': 2523}
