overed, and the second task includes the template, file mode, and variable file. Looks good.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: group | Manage group {{ group.name }}\n  group:\n    name: "{{ group.name }}"\n    state: present\n    gid: "{{ group.gid | default(\'\') }}"\n    system: yes\n\n- name: group | Set sudo options for group {{ group.name }}\n  template:\n    src: group_sudoers.j2\n    dest: /etc/sudoers.d/{{ group.name }}\n    mode: 0o0440\n    remote_src: yes\n  vars_files:\n    - group_sudo_vars.yml\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-19T17:28:47.087597204Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 11758895031, 'load_duration': 73712507, 'prompt_eval_count': 324, 'prompt_eval_duration': 95874348, 'eval_count': 577, 'eval_duration': 11587918335, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--679f9b36-9dd3-45c8-ba81-db2d4e7a6175-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 324, 'output_tokens': 577, 'total_tokens': 901}
