rd in the playbook, so I should include `become: true` in the task.\n\nWait, but the `a2enmod` command isn\'t a package; it\'s a script that enables modules. So maybe using `ansible.builtin.command` with `become: true` is better here. Because `a2enmod` is a shell script, and using `command` is more appropriate than `shell` because `command` is more suited for executing commands directly, and it\'s more idempotent when using `changed_when` properly.\n\nSo, perhaps I should use `ansible.builtin.command` for enabling the modules. Let me adjust that. So, the task becomes using `command` module with `argv: [\'a2enmod\', \'proxy\', \'proxy_http\']` and `become: true`. This should make the task more idempotent because `command` is better than `shell` for such tasks.\n\nThen, for the second task, it\'s already using `template`, which is good. The loop is correctly set up, and the notifies are in place. The only thing is to ensure that the `notify` is correctly indented under the task.\n\nSo, putting it all together, I\'ll replace the first task\'s `shell` with `command`, set `become: true`, and ensure that the module is correctly called. This should fix both linting issues: using shell and the idempotency problem.\n\nI also need to make sure that the playbook structure is correct, starting with `---` and each task properly formatted. No extra comments or explanations should be added, just the corrected YAML.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: locations | Enable modules\n  ansible.builtin.command:\n    argv: [\'a2enmod\', \'proxy\', \'proxy_http\']\n    become: true\n  notify: httpd-restart\n\n- name: locations | Configure locations\n  ansible.builtin.template:\n    dest: "{{ apache_location_dir }}/{{ item.name }}.conf"\n    mode: 420\n  loop: "{{ httpd_locations }}"\n  notify:\n    - httpd-configtest\n    - httpd-restart\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-19T17:32:15.565415907Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'sto