content='<think>\nAlright, I need to figure out how to generate an Ansible Playbook based on the given tasks. Let\'s start by understanding the requirements.\n\nFirst, the playbook must adhere strictly to the instructions. It should begin with \'---\' on the first line and conform to yamllint and ansible-lint standards. It\'s meant to be included in an Ansible Role, so the structure should be appropriate for tasks/ directory, like tasks/main.yml.\n\nThe user provided two tasks. Task 1 is to create the document root for each vhost. So, I need a task that loops over httpd_vhosts, checks if documentroot is defined and create_docroot isn\'t set to false. The directory should be created with 0755 permissions.\n\nFor Task 2, each vhost needs to have its configuration file templated. The template file is {{ vhost_conf_template }}, and it should be saved in httpd_vhosts_directory with the vhost\'s name as the filename. The file mode should be 0644. Additionally, after configuring, it should notify the Test httpd configuration validity and Restart httpd handlers.\n\nI\'ll structure the playbook with two tasks. The first task uses file module with state=directory and creates the directory only if conditions are met. The second task uses template module, loops over httpd_vhosts, and notifies the appropriate handlers.\n\nI need to ensure that the tasks are correctly ordered and that all parameters match the descriptions. Also, I shouldn\'t include any playbook-level headers like hosts or vars, just the tasks.\n\nPutting it all together, the playbook starts with \'---\', then lists the tasks with their respective modules, arguments, and notifications. I\'ll make sure the YAML syntax is correct, using proper indentation and no extraneous comments or explanations.\n\nFinally, I\'ll double-check that each task is exactly as specified, with no additions or omissions. The output should be a valid YAML playbook that fits into an Ansible Role\'s tasks directory.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Create docroot for each vhost\n  file:\n    path: "{{ item.documentroot }}"\n    state: directory\n    mode: \'0755\'\n  loop: "{{ httpd_vhosts | default([]) | list }}"\n  when:\n    - item.documentroot is defined\n    - item.create_docroot | default(true) | bool\n\n- name: Configure vhosts\n  template:\n    src: "{{ vhost_conf_template }}"\n    dest: "{{ httpd_vhosts_directory }}/{{ item.name }}.conf"\n    mode: \'0644\'\n  loop: "{{ httpd_vhosts | default([]) | list }}"\n  notify:\n    - Test httpd configuration validity\n    - Restart httpd\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-19T17:33:36.876362247Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 9650220241, 'load_duration': 99447482, 'prompt_eval_count': 381, 'prompt_eval_duration': 80755743, 'eval_count': 570, 'eval_duration': 9469380753, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--f7b97291-7aed-40a8-9883-246bf9fb74a4-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 381, 'output_tokens': 570, 'total_tokens': 951}
