content='<think>\nOkay, I need to fix the Ansible playbook so that it passes ansible-lint. Let me look at the errors reported and figure out what needs to be changed.\n\nFirst, the error messages mention using FQCN for certain modules. I see that the modules import_tasks, apt, shell, and template are being used without their full class names. So I should replace them with their FQCNs. That means changing import_tasks to ansible.builtin.import_tasks, apt to ansible.builtin.apt, shell to ansible.builtin.shell, and template to ansible.builtin.template.\n\nNext, there\'s a warning about using shell instead of command. The task \'Find used php.ini\' uses shell, but it\'s just running a command without any shell processing. So I should switch that to the command module. This will also fix the \'no-changed-when\' warning because the command module is idempotent by default.\n\nAnother issue is the octal value 0644. Ansible lint doesn\'t like implicit octal values. I should convert 0644 to decimal, which is 420, and use that instead.\n\nLet me go through each task:\n\n1. Import assertion tasks: Change to ansible.builtin.import_tasks.\n2. Install php: Change apt to ansible.builtin.apt.\n3. Find php.ini: Replace shell with command and adjust the module parameters to get the path.\n4. Configure php: Use ansible.builtin.template and set mode to 420.\n\nI also need to make sure that the variables and task names stay the same. The \'when\' conditions should remain as they are.\n\nI think these changes should address all the linting issues without altering the intended functionality of the playbook.\n</think>\n\n---\n- name: Import assertion tasks\n  ansible.builtin.import_tasks:\n    file: assert.yml\n  args:\n    run_once: true\n  delegate_to: localhost\n\n- name: Install php\n  ansible.builtin.apt:\n    name: "{{ php_packages }}"\n    state: present\n\n- name: Find used php.ini\n  ansible.builtin.command:\n    cmd: php --ini\n  register: php_found_ini_location\n  when: php_ini_location is not defined\n\n- name: Configure php\n  ansible.builtin.template:\n    src: php.ini.j2\n    dest: "{{ php_found_ini_location.path }}"\n    mode: 420\n  notify: Restart httpd\n  when: php_found_ini_location is defined' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-19T18:00:31.987210864Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 12277612226, 'load_duration': 93774000, 'prompt_eval_count': 2293, 'prompt_eval_duration': 1363434047, 'eval_count': 515, 'eval_duration': 10819380028, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--2137191a-bed5-49b5-a3e4-3cb24b329fe6-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2293, 'output_tokens': 515, 'total_tokens': 2808}
