 correct names, modules, and variables. Also, the playbook shouldn\'t include any hosts, vars, or playbook-level headers. It should be a list of tasks only, suitable for an Ansible Role\'s tasks/main.yml.\n\nI should also check that the YAML is valid, maybe using yamllint and ansible-lint. But since I\'m writing it manually, I\'ll just have to be careful with the syntax.\n\nPutting it all together, I\'ll structure each task with the correct parameters, making sure variables are properly referenced and conditions are added where necessary.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  import_tasks: assert.yml\n  run_once: true\n  host: localhost\n\n- name: Uninstall systemd-logger\n  apt:\n    name: systemd-logger\n    state: absent\n\n- name: Install rsyslog\n  apt:\n    name: "{{ rsyslog_packages }}"\n    state: "{{ rsyslog_package_state }}"\n\n- name: Install additional rsyslog packages\n  apt:\n    name: "{{ item }}"\n    state: present\n  loop: "{{ rsyslog_features }}"\n\n- name: Configure default rsyslog\n  template:\n    src: "{{ rsyslog_config_file_format }}"\n    dest: "{{ rsyslog_dest_conf_file }}"\n  notify: Restart rsyslog\n\n- name: Make configuration directory\n  file:\n    path: /etc/rsyslog.d/\n    state: directory\n    mode: 0755\n\n- name: Configure rsyslog forward rule\n  template:\n    src: forward_rule.conf.j2\n    dest: /etc/rsyslog.d/{{ rsyslog_forward_rule_name }}.conf\n  notify: Restart rsyslog\n  when: rsyslog_deploy_default_config is false\n\n- name: Configuring additional config files\n  copy:\n    src: "{{ item.key }}"\n    dest: /etc/rsyslog.d/\n    remote_src: yes\n  loop: "{{ rsyslog_rsyslog_d_files.items() }}"\n  when: item.value.state is present\n  notify: Restart rsyslog\n\n- name: Start and enable rsyslog\n  service:\n    name: "{{ rsyslog_service }}"\n    state: started\n    enabled: yes\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-19T19:11:46.425860452Z', 'done': True,